摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Desktop computer use for DeepSeek Harness: macOS app listing, accessibility-tree window capture, screenshots, and synthesized input, cloned from Codex Computer Use","id":"gh:1334278646","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-computer-use","slug":"geohotstan/dsh-computer-use","topics":["codex","computer-use","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","macos"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Desktop computer use for DeepSeek Harness: macOS app listing, accessibility-tree window capture, scr"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"eenshots, and synthesized input, cloned from Codex Computer Use"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# @zibokapi/dsh-codex-computer-use"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A standalone plugin for the DeepSeek Harness: desktop computer use on macOS — app listing, key-windo"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"w capture as a screenshot plus model-readable accessibility tree, and synthesized mouse and keyboard"},{"id":"p4s3","text":" input — cloned from OpenAI's Codex Computer Use window API. Input delivery is background-first like"},{"id":"p4s4","text":" Codex's own execution model: semantic AX actions need no focus, and raw events ride the private Sky"},{"id":"p4s5","text":"Light path (`SLEventPostToPid` with the keyboard authentication envelope, field stamps, and focus-wi"},{"id":"p4s6","text":"thout-raise records, ported from the MIT-licensed trycua/cua project) with a public `CGEvent.postToP"},{"id":"p4s7","text":"id` fallback per symbol, so the user's foreground never changes. It needs no OpenAI components."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"The design is accessibility-tree-first: `computer_use_get_app_state` returns a numbered, tab-indente"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"d element tree; the model acts on element indexes, with window-relative coordinates as a fallback, a"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"nd later captures of the same app return diffs instead of the full tree."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Everything ships in this one package: the seam, the local Swift-daemon provider, the `computer_use_*"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"` tools, the approval policy, and a standalone MCP server. The complete feature delta against OpenAI"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"'s implementation lives in docs/codex-parity.md; that reference is the parity checklist."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"This repository is a DSH bundle: the root `package.json` declares `dsh.bundle.patch` → `cordis.patch"},{"id":"p8s2","text":".yml`, which inserts the three host rows under this package's own subpaths (`@zibokapi/dsh-codex-com"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"puter-use/*`). One install brings everything."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Step 2 is the only macOS-specific part. It builds the Swift helper from the `native/` directory ship"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ped inside the installed package (Xcode Command Line Tools required — `xcode-select --install`), bun"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"dles and signs it into `~/.dsh/computer-use/dsh-computer-daemon.app`, then explicitly asks for the t"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"wo permissions the daemon needs — **Accessibility** and **Screen Recording** — through the macOS sys"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"tem dialogs, polling until the grants land. It writes no configuration and none is needed: with `hel"},{"id":"p10s6","text":"perPath` unset, the engine falls back to that exact path."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The install location is stable on purpose. macOS TCC keys each grant on the helper's bundle id, code"},{"id":"p11s2","text":" signature, and on-disk path; a path inside `node_modules` would change with every plugin update, so"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" the daemon lives under the DSH home (`$DSH_HOME/computer-use`) and the grants survive plugin update"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"he daemon lives under the DSH home (`$DSH_HOME/computer-use`) and the grants survive plugin updates."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"dsh re-asks for the grants whenever the plugin loads: a missing or revoked grant simply means comput"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"er use is not loaded until it is granted (the daemon opens the matching System Settings pane on a re"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"membered denial). `dsh-codex-computer-use status` reports the install at any time."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The registry tarball ships `lib/`, and `lib/` is committed to git, so every install form — npm, a gi"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"t URL, a packed tarball — works without running any build script (`pnpm` ≥10 blocks lifecycle script"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"s of git-hosted dependencies by default, so the built entries ship in the repository itself)."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### Lazy path"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Tell your dsh:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"then run steps 2–3 above (`npx @zibokapi/dsh-codex-computer-use`, restart the profile)."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### Manual (from a checkout)"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"`dsh plugin add` registers the repo as a bundle layer in the profile (`dsh.profile.bundles`). The en"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"gine resolves the daemon in order: the `helperPath` config → the `DSH_COMPUTER_HELPER_PATH` environm"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"ent override → the setup CLI's install location (`~/.dsh/computer-use/dsh-computer-daemon.app/Conten"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"ts/MacOS/dsh-computer-daemon`). Set `helperPath` only to point at a custom build."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Entries"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"One package, five subpath entries (plus the invariant companions under `./<entry>/invariant`):"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| Entry | Role | Loader row |"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"| `./computer` | Service Definition — `ctx.computer` | registered by `computer-local` |\n| `./compute"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"r-local` | Local provider — resident Swift daemon (AX tree, screenshots, CGEvent input) | `@zibokapi"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"/dsh-codex-computer-use/computer-local` |\n| `./computer-tools` | The `computer_use_*` tools plus the"},{"id":"p24s4","text":" `computer-use` skill | `@zibokapi/dsh-codex-computer-use/computer-tools` |\n| `./computer-policy` | "},{"id":"p24s5","text":"Per-app approval gate + Codex-style tier guidance + `computer_use_list_granted_applications` | `@zib"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"okapi/dsh-codex-computer-use/computer-policy` |\n| `./computer-mcp` | Standalone MCP stdio server exp"},{"id":"p24s7","text":"osing the same surface for external MCP clients | not a loader row — a binary |"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Compose"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Authoring a composition by hand uses the same subpaths:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"`helperPath` is optional — the engine falls back to the setup CLI's install location — and the other"},{"id":"p28s2","text":" rows are optional too (`@zibokapi/dsh-codex-computer-use/computer-policy` needs an approval service"},{"id":"p28s3","text":" mounted, e.g. `@deepseek-ai/dsh-user-approval`). A runnable composition lives in `example/cordis.ym"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"unted, e.g. `@deepseek-ai/dsh-user-approval`). A runnable composition lives in `example/cordis.yml`."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## MCP server"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"The `@zibokapi/dsh-codex-computer-use/computer-mcp` bin exposes the same surface — the official ten "},{"id":"p30s2","text":"Codex Computer Use window tools plus `request_access` and the three `event_stream_*` recording tools"},{"id":"p30s3","text":" — as a standalone MCP stdio server over the same engine, so Codex CLI, Claude Code, or any MCP clie"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"nt can drive the harness's computer use. The bin keeps the harness packages external like every othe"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"r entry (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-subprocess-local` ships node-pty, a native module that cannot be bundled)"},{"id":"p30s6","text":", so it runs wherever `pnpm install` has materialized the dependencies:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"The server speaks newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 on stdin/stdout, answers `initialize` / `ping` / `t"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"ools/list` / `tools/call`, and mirrors the official response behavior: action tools answer with the "},{"id":"p32s3","text":"post-action state (text plus a JPEG image block when one was captured)."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Permissions"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"## Develop"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## Verification"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"- CI `check` job (Ubuntu): a clean `pnpm install` from npm — the user-facing path — then typecheck a"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"nd build against the published `@deepseek-ai/*` packages.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"MIT — see LICENSE."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
